From: Scott Quarrier <squarrier@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:44:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] glm5_next/cuda: waiting prompts share a prompt chunk,
 TF_GLM_MULTI_PREFILL (MiaAI-Lab recipe patch 0049)

MiaAI-Lab's recipe (github.com/MiaAI-Lab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-2x-DGX-Sparks-TensorFold @ 1576746, with
TF_GLM_MULTI_PREFILL=1 in its config) fills the prompts of concurrent requests together: one prompt chunk holds the
next rows of several waiting prompts, back to back. Under --parallel, PR #243's engine fills them one stream at a
time with a decode round between chunks, so the last of four short prompts that arrive together waits for eight
forwards (four when undrafted). This ports recipe patch 0049-glm-multi-prefill (Apache License 2.0, Copyright 2026
MiaAI-Lab):

- multi_prefill.py (new) is the recipe's file: the settings (TF_GLM_MULTI_PREFILL, TF_GLM_MULTI_PREFILL_WAIT_MS),
  Piece, layout (a shared slot, overlapping extents or too many rows are refused), PieceMixer and prefill_pieces.
  The row-independent work (embedding, glue, the blocks' fronts and output projections, router, routed and shared
  experts, the final norm) runs once over every row; what reads or writes a stream's own state runs piece by piece
  through the calls a chunk of its own makes, so each prompt's rows get the bits they get alone.
- forward.py: kda_block's and _dsa_latent's stream-state parts become kda_rows and dsa_rows, their fronts kda_front
  and dsa_front (row ranges). kda_block and dsa_block call them for a chunk of their own (rows 0 .. R), so without
  the setting the forward makes the calls it made before. compute(head=False) leaves the final norm's rows for the
  per-piece head. The recipe's edits to its tensor-parallel _compute prefetch and split_layers are not taken; the
  layer loop's existing mixer hook carries PieceMixer.
- multi.py (PR #243's engine): rank 0 groups filling streams (_group: foreground first, then the fewest prompt rows
  left, then admission order; each to its next kept point or its end, or the budget left in multiples of 64 rows,
  within the single-stream row budget). The MFILL op carries the group inside rank 0's sealed message; rank 1 checks
  each stop against its kept points before it fills (_fill_many). Streams drafting with the MTP head fill alone.
  /health counts rank 0's multi-prompt chunks. GlmScheduler._admit can wait TF_GLM_MULTI_PREFILL_WAIT_MS on an idle
  server for requests arriving together.
- engine.py: the --parallel startup line names the setting; the AFD check reads both settings before the wire opens.

On the attention/expert split a multi-prompt chunk is one prompt-chunk forward of at most the expert nodes'
prefill_rows rows (the settings handshake's), behind one begin(R, chunk=True): the expert nodes need no change and
the wire is unchanged. The setting is off unless TF_GLM_MULTI_PREFILL is set (the recipe's config turns it on);
unset, the replies, cached counts and kept states are the ones before, and the forward's kernel calls are the same.

Tests: tests/test_glm_multi_prefill.py (CPU: the settings, layout's refusals, staging and the experts' prefill_rows;
PR #243's fake model grouped against ungrouped at two ranks, at world 1 over the fake AFD wire, with TF_GLM_KV=fp8's
rings and with TF_GLM_SHARED_PREFIX's points: replies against the requests served alone, kept states and their pool
rows; a burst of four short prompts in two prompt forwards instead of eight; rank 1's refusal; MTP streams; the idle
server's wait; the real forward with PieceMixer over recorded kernels, each piece's calls those of its own chunk).
tests/test_glm_multi.py and test_glm_multi_afd.py: the fake model runs a multi-prompt chunk's pieces.

Credit: THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md ("GLM multi-prompt prefill") and the ported functions' comments name MiaAI-Lab and
the patch.

